rlando, Florida.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Cameron  Pforr | CFO & CEO | Compensation: $313,651 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 239 people. Revenue per employee of $228K ranks in the bottom quartile among Technology peers, with revenue growing 20%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $34K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["M-tron Industries, Inc. is a micro-cap technology business with a $280M market cap on $54M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +3.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 25% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 15-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $8M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 15 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.26\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 5.7% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 22% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.2244467221627671},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 9.9% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"AI disruption of existing software moats \u2014 incumbents with durable margins face commoditisation as AI-native competitors replicate features at a fraction of the R&D cost.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 25% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Operating margins 12% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"M-tron Industries (MPTI) Q3 2026 Earnings Call Transcript","source":"fool.com","link":"https://www.fool.com/earnings/call-transcripts/2026/11/13/m-tron-industries-mpti-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/?source=iedfolrf0000001","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794546820.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Avoiding Lag: Real-Time Signals in (MPTI) Movement","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/35/Avoiding_Lag:_Real-Time_Signals_in_MPTI_Movement_111226015401_1794509641.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794509641.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.823,"